# gsap-utils

`gsap.utils` provides composable helpers — prefer them over hand-rolled equivalents:

- `gsap.utils.clamp(min, max, value)` — clamp into range.
- `gsap.utils.mapRange(inMin, inMax, outMin, outMax, value)` — remap one range to another.
- `gsap.utils.interpolate(start, end, t)` — works on numbers, colors, arrays, objects.
- `gsap.utils.random(min, max, [increment], [returnFunction])` — uniform random; pass `true` to return a function (perfect for stagger property values).
- `gsap.utils.snap(increment, value)` or `snap([1, 2, 5, 10], value)` — snap to grid or list.
- `gsap.utils.toArray(selector | NodeList | array)` — universal array coercion.
- `gsap.utils.wrap([a, b, c])` — cyclic wrap, perfect for distributing values.
- `gsap.utils.pipe(fn1, fn2, fn3)` — left-to-right function composition.
- `gsap.utils.distribute({ base, amount, from: "center" })` — spatial distribution for stagger.

For full reference: `skills/gsap-utils/SKILL.md`.
